DESERT SURVIVAL TRAINING SYLLABUS -- SUNA ACADEMY & GENIN CORPS

No enemy kills more Sand shinobi than the desert itself. This syllabus is
mandatory before any recruit is cleared for cross-dune deployment.

Module 1 -- Water discipline: Recognize dehydration; ration per the Water
Ration Policy; never drink from unverified oases. A shinobi who wastes water
endangers the squad.
Module 2 -- Heat and cold: The dunes scorch by day and freeze by night. Robe
layering, shade discipline, and travel timing (dawn/dusk marches) are drilled.
Module 3 -- Navigation: Reading dunes, stars, and wind direction; the sands
shift and erase trails, so landmarks are unreliable.
Module 4 -- Sandstorm protocol: Seal eyes and mouth, anchor low, wait it out.
Wind-users may disperse minor storms; none may fight a major one.
Module 5 -- Scorpion, snake, and heat-hazard first aid; coordinate with the
medical corps' heat-exposure log.

Assessment: A supervised three-day dune crossing. Failure returns the recruit
to Academy conditioning.
